# Flow JSON authoring guide

Shape below matches **`projects/CMS/**/flows/*.flow.json`** in this repo (see e.g. **`add-an-environment.flow.json`**, **`delete-content-type.flow.json`**, **`get-started-with-workflows.flow.json`**). Fields are illustrative placeholders—replace **`id`**, **`source`**, **`module`**, and step **`target`** strings with your doc’s values.

```json
{
  "id": "cms-authoring-example",
  "project": "CMS",
  "module": "content-models",
  "stage": "main",
  "source": "https://www.contentstack.com/docs/developers/create-content-types/delete-a-content-type",
  "type": "executable",
  "use": ["login", "selectStack"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "action": "verify",
      "target": "Confirm Delete",
      "expected": { "within": "Modal", "labelEquals": "Confirm Delete" }
    },
    {
      "action": "click",
      "target": "vertical ellipsis",
      "expected": { "rowContains": "AUTO-" }
    }
  ]
}
```

- **`use`:** Often `login` only or `["login", "selectStack"]` like real CMS flows (see **`add-an-environment.flow.json`** vs **`delete-content-type.flow.json`**).
- **Verify step:** Doc-named **`target`** plus **`expected.within`** when the doc states placement; **`labelEquals`** matches the doc’s exact wording. Real flows sometimes add **`withinStrict`** or **`labelMatch`**—for doc-derived checks follow **`doc-step-parity.mdc`**.
- **Row menu:** Reuse the **same** **`expected.rowContains`** on every later ⋯ / **Delete** (etc.) step for that row—see **`flow-row-action-menu-rowcontains.mdc`**.

## Multi-part docs

Split into **`projects/.../flows/<id>-part-1.flow.json`**, **`<id>-part-2.flow.json`**, each with its **`.selectors.ts`**—see **`doc-parts-one-file-per-part.mdc`**.

## Do not

- Add steps the document does **not** describe (no inferred “fix the UI” steps).
- Use loose **contains** / **`labelMatch`** for **doc-named** UI verification where **`doc-step-parity.mdc`** requires **`labelEquals`**.
